ream flooding caused by excessive rainfall\ncontinues.\n\n* WHERE...West Central Montezuma County in southwestern Colorado...\nSoutheastern San Juan County in southeastern Utah...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1045 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring. Streams\ncontinue to rise due to excess runoff from earlier rainfall.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 837 PM MDT, River gages indicate high flow through McElmo\nCanyon and water levels continue to rise. Flooding is ongoing or\nexpected to begin shortly in the warned area.\n- This includes but is not limited to the following streams\nanddrainages...\nFlorida River, Spring Creek, Ute Creek, Salt Creek and Dry Creek.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nLow-lying areas along McElmo Creek between Cortez and Aneth.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-22T22:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Montezuma, CO; San Juan, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d1616bea532703e8b3755c48a98fe0adbdb19a4d.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d1616bea532703e8b3755c48a98fe0adbdb19a4d.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 22 at 1:49PM MDT until October 23 at 12:00PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, Animas River Basin, Four Corners/Upper Dolores River, San\nJuan River Basin and Southwest San Juan Mountains and Utah,\nincluding the following areas, Arches/Grand Flat,\nCanyonlands/Natural Bridges, La Sal and Abajo Mountains and\nSoutheast Utah.\n\n* WHEN...Through Friday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, recent burn scars and other low-lying and\nflood-prone locations. Low-water crossings may be flooded. Storm\ndrains and ditches ma